WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
In 1889, the Shah Jahan
Mosque opened in Woking.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.630
Britain already had
small Muslim communities.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:14.080
In the 1950s and 60s, men from Pakistan and
India came to work in mills and foundries.

4
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.930
Many planned to go home.

5
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.380
Instead, they stayed, and communities
grew in towns and cities across Britain.

6
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.910
Can British Muslims
keep their faith whole,

7
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.460
and still belong fully in Britain?

8
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.850
In this mission, you'll trace how small
groups of workers and seamen grew into

9
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.990
communities across Britain.

10
00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.410
Then you'll meet the many
groups inside British Islam:

11
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.580
different roots, different
traditions, different generations.

12
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.080
Your mission: weigh up whether British
Muslims can keep their faith whole and

13
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.680
still belong fully.
